  "question": {
    "text": "A perpendicular is drawn from a point on the line <math><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> to the plane <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math> such that the foot of the perpendicular <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> also lies on the plane <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Then the coordinates of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> are"
  },
